'''orbisRPC''' is a free, [[open-source software|open-source]] [[Discord]] [[Rich Presence]] utility for the [[PlayStation 4]]. It runs as a payload on [[GoldHEN]]-jailbroken consoles and displays the game currently being played — title, cover art and a play timer — on a user's Discord profile.<ref name="repo">{{cite web |title=orbisRPC repository |url=https://github.com/SirHumza/orbisRPC |access-date=18 October 2026}}</ref> Unlike earlier PlayStation 4 rich-presence tools, which are PC-side scripts, orbisRPC runs entirely on the console and connects directly to the Discord gateway over [[Transport Layer Security|TLS]].<ref name="repo" />

== Features ==

orbisRPC detects the foreground application on the console and reports it to Discord. Coverage includes retail PlayStation 4 titles, homebrew software, and a curated list of PlayStation, PlayStation 2 and PlayStation Portable titles, with automatic cover art drawn from image databases.<ref name="repo" />

The software supports [[PlayStation 4 system software|firmware]] versions 5.05 through 13.52, and is installed as a single package that can start automatically on boot.<ref name="repo" />

